.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH orbit-completions 1  "completions " 
.SH NAME
orbit\-completions \- Print shell completions to stdout
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBorbit completions\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISHELL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print shell completions to stdout
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one JSON object per result, with `"v":1`, instead of text
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable ANSI colors
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISHELL\fR>
The shell to write completions for
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
bash
.IP \(bu 2
elvish
.IP \(bu 2
fish
.IP \(bu 2
powershell
.IP \(bu 2
zsh
.RE
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  orbit completions bash > ~/.local/share/bash\-completion/completions/orbit
  orbit completions zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_orbit"
  orbit completions fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/orbit.fish
